readings.c2s1:
explained by reason or by the knowledge possessed; inexplicable; hence, strange.
{{smaller block|As ''unaccountable'' as one would think it, a wise man is not always a good man. {{right|''Steele'', Spectator, No. 6.}}}}
{{smaller block|Nothing is more ''unaccountable'' than the spell that often lurks in a spoken word. {{right|''Hawthorne'', Marble Faun, xxv.}}}}
'''2.''' Not subject to account or control; not subject to answer; not responsible.
{{smaller block|Hee met at first with Doctrines of ''unaccountable'' Prerogative; in them hee rested, because they pleas’d him. {{right|''Milton'', Eikonoklastes, xi.}}}}
