'''unaccountableness''' (un-a̤-koun′ta̤-bl-nes), ''n.'' '''1.''' The state or character of being unaccountable, or incapable of being explained or accounted for.
{{smaller block|The ''unaccountableness'' of this theory. {{right|''Glanville.''}}}}
'''2.''' The character or state of being not subject to account or control; irresponsibility.
{{smaller block|An ''unaccountableness'', in practice and conversation, to the rules and terms of their own communion. {{right|''Penn'', Rise and Progress of Quakers, iv.}}}}

'''unaccountably''' (un-a̤-koun′ta̤-bli), ''adv.'' In an unaccountable manner; strangely.

